# Jarvis — secrets, generated data, and machine noise.
#
# The one rule this file exists to enforce: **`.env` never gets committed.**
# It holds a live LLM_API_KEY and a GDTF Share account and password, in
# plaintext, by design. `.env.example` is the committed template and carries
# no real values.
#
# Verify after changing anything here:
#     git status --porcelain --ignored | findstr /C:"!! .env"
# and before every push:
#     git ls-files | findstr /i "env$ session token"
# A credential in git history stays there even if you delete it later, so the
# check has to happen BEFORE the first commit, not after.

# ---- secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
secrets/
*.secret

# ---- the fixture library and anything derived from an account -----------
# data/ is regenerated at run time and is not source.  It holds the local
# fixture database, the downloaded GDTF Share cache (which contains a live
# session cookie and vendor files published under their own terms), the
# autosaved show state, saved show files and 976 generated patch CSVs.
#
# The .gdtf rule is deliberate and separate: those files come from GDTF
# Share under a free account for YOUR use.  Redistributing them in a public
# repository is a licensing question, not a technical one, so they are
# excluded by name wherever they land rather than relying on data/ alone.
data/
*.gdtf
*.gdTF
fixtures_inbox/
*.mrd
*.pgz
fixtures.db*
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# session cookies and anything a login produced
*session*.txt
*session*.json
*.cookie
cookies.txt

# ---- the operator's own show -------------------------------------------
# Your rig, your venues, your show files.  Not mine to publish.
*.mrk
*.shw
*.sbk
autosave.json
showsettings.ini
*.csv            # generated patch exports - data/patch/ alone is 976 files

# ---- python --------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/

# ---- editors / OS --------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ---- logs and scratch -----------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
tmp/
temp/
scratch/

# docs/backup holds my working copies of the docs, kept so an accidental
# truncation is recoverable.  They are duplicates of files that are already
# tracked, and a repository is the wrong place to keep a backup of itself.
docs/backup/

# ---- credentials that live in shell history or a venv -------------------
.history
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc

# ...except the design skills' own data tables (ui-ux-pro-max, design,
# design-system): third-party MIT data, see .claude/skills/_licenses/
!.claude/skills/*/data/
!.claude/skills/*/data/**
